  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Boot and the fast path",
      "items": [
        "--version and --help never load the engine, the SDK or the TUI: the startup budget in CI is measured on exactly that path",
        "the mode router decides once — tui, print, json, stream or command — and the container (config, secret store, SDK, output port, clock) is built lazily afterwards",
        "the mode router is also where the TTY is checked: an interactive mode on a pipe refuses with an actionable message instead of hanging on a prompt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The terminal guard",
      "items": [
        "the cleanup is registered before the raw mode is entered, and it restores the cursor, the alternate screen, the mouse tracking, the bracketed paste and the title",
        "the guard runs on exit, on SIGINT, on SIGTERM and on an uncaught exception — a crash leaves the terminal usable, not raw",
        "in a non-TTY the guard is a no-op: a piped run emits no escape sequence and no prompt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The endings",
      "items": [
        "the exit code is the contract: 0 success, 2 usage, 3 authentication, 4 forbidden, 5 not found, 8 rate limited, 9 network, 10 server, 130 SIGINT, 143 SIGTERM",
        "a crash prints one line on stderr; the stack is behind --debug, and the terminal is restored before the process dies",
        "EPIPE ends the run quietly with 0 when the consumer closed the pipe — a broken pipe is not a crash",
        "no process.exit deep in the code: the command returns the code and the process sets it"
      ]
    }
  ]
